<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system repurchases.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system repurchases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Thursday through overnight system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts had anticipated a reserve addition through either overnight or term system repurchase agreements.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate, at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>-- ((North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
